From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0410: export nfsmw_cp_event_seq from rexgpu-xenos.dll, bumped and woken on every CP fence write

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (W3.2). The idea is $IOS games/mcla/sdk_patches/0207-cp-event-seq-fence-wake.patch
  redone for Win32 (WakeByAddressAll instead of futex / os_sync_wake_by_address_all); the symbol, its places in the
  command processor and the wake protocol are the same, nothing is copied
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: rexgpu-xenos.dll exports the C data symbol `nfsmw_cp_event_seq` (std::atomic<uint32_t>), which the command
  processor increments and WakeByAddressAll's after each guest memory write a fence can ride on (EVENT_WRITE_SHD,
  MEM_WRITE, a matched COND_WRITE, REG_TO_MEM). mcla/hooks/mcla_fence_spin.cpp resolves it with GetProcAddress and
  WaitOnAddress'es on it. Links Synchronization.lib. No cvar, no change for the guest. Not built before the first W3 build.
Bucket: REDO

0410-cp-event-seq-export.patch (mcla-x86 W3.2; redoes the idea of $IOS 0207 for Windows)

Purpose. The game's D3D fence poll (sub_82412F98, hooked by mcla/hooks/mcla_fence_spin.cpp) spins on a fence word the
command processor writes with PM4 EVENT_WRITE_SHD. Without a word to sleep on, the hook can only Sleep(1) between polls
(a fence noticed up to 1 ms late, 1,000 wakes a second); with one, the thread sleeps until the command processor has
written the fence and is woken at once, and a poll that times out becomes the exception.

Change (src/graphics/command_processor.cpp, Windows only; elsewhere NfsmwCpPublishEvent() is an empty function):
  * `extern "C" __declspec(dllexport) std::atomic<uint32_t> nfsmw_cp_event_seq{0};` in the plugin. It is a VARIABLE:
    GetProcAddress(rexgpu-xenos.dll, "nfsmw_cp_event_seq") is its address, which is how the hook casts it
    (reinterpret_cast<std::atomic<uint32_t>*>(GetProcAddress(...))). Exported with __declspec because the plugin is built
    with hidden visibility. Not in rexruntime.dll: the command processor is in the plugin (the hook looks in the plugin
    first, in rexruntime second).
  * NfsmwCpPublishEvent(): fetch_add(1, release) then WakeByAddressAll(&nfsmw_cp_event_seq), called right AFTER the
    guest memory store, so a waiter that sees the new value sees the store. Called after: ExecutePacketType3_EVENT_WRITE_SHD
    (the D3D fence: counter or value written to the packet's address), ExecutePacketType3_MEM_WRITE (after its loop),
    ExecutePacketType3_COND_WRITE (when it matched and wrote memory), ExecutePacketType3_REG_TO_MEM. Not after
    EVENT_WRITE_EXT (fake screen extents), EVENT_WRITE_ZPD (occlusion counts: another poll) or register writes.
    D3D12 and Vulkan share these handlers (neither overrides them).
  * src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt: rexgpu-xenos links Synchronization on Windows (WakeByAddressAll).
Cost: one atomic add plus one WakeByAddressAll per fence write (a few a frame); expected to enter the kernel only when
it wakes a waiter (not measured).

Not built or run (clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only of the TU with the SDK's Release flags: the same 40 diagnostics as before,
none new; a -c object carries `/EXPORT:nfsmw_cp_event_seq,DATA` and an undefined WakeByAddressAll).
Verify: `dumpbin /exports rexgpu-xenos.dll | findstr nfsmw_cp_event_seq`, and the hook's log line
`[mcla-fence-spin] waits on nfsmw_cp_event_seq` (not the WARN `not found`).

---
diff --git a/src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt b/src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt
index fc8a81c0..a43d2be6 100644
--- a/src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -197,3 +197,8 @@ endif()
 if(WIN32)
     target_link_libraries(rexgpu-xenos PRIVATE avrt)
 endif()
+
+# LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410): nfsmw_cp_event_seq wakes its waiters with WakeByAddressAll (Synchronization.lib).
+if(WIN32)
+    target_link_libraries(rexgpu-xenos PRIVATE Synchronization)
+endif()
diff --git a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
index cb0a2bd1..60246b5a 100644
--- a/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/command_processor.cpp
@@ -43,6 +43,19 @@
 #include <rex/ui/low_latency.h>
 #include <rex/ui/presenter.h>
 
+#if REX_PLATFORM_WIN32
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410): WakeByAddressAll for nfsmw_cp_event_seq (Synchronization.lib).
+#ifndef NOMINMAX
+#define NOMINMAX
+#endif
+#ifndef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#endif
+#include <windows.h>
+
+#include <atomic>
+#endif
+
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(vsync, true, "GPU", "Enable vertical sync");
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_INT32(shader_storage_progress, 0, "GPU",
                      "While stored pipelines are created at start, print a progress line on "
@@ -263,6 +276,26 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(async_pipeline_end_of_frame_wait, false, "GPU",
                     "left out either way.")
     .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410): the fence-write sequence, exported by rexgpu-xenos.dll as the C symbol
+// `nfsmw_cp_event_seq` (a std::atomic<uint32_t> variable; GetProcAddress gives its address). The command processor
+// bumps it and wakes every WaitOnAddress waiter after each memory write it makes for the guest that a fence can ride
+// on (EVENT_WRITE_SHD, MEM_WRITE, a matched COND_WRITE, REG_TO_MEM), so the game's D3D fence poll (the hook
+// mcla_fence_spin in the game layer) sleeps until the fence is written instead of spinning or polling on a timeout.
+#if REX_PLATFORM_WIN32
+extern "C" __declspec(dllexport) std::atomic<uint32_t> nfsmw_cp_event_seq{0};
+namespace {
+inline void NfsmwCpPublishEvent() {
+  // After the guest memory store the caller just made: a waiter that sees the new value sees the store.
+  nfsmw_cp_event_seq.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_release);
+  WakeByAddressAll(&nfsmw_cp_event_seq);
+}
+}  // namespace
+#else
+namespace {
+inline void NfsmwCpPublishEvent() {}
+}  // namespace
+#endif
+
 namespace rex::graphics {
 
 using namespace rex::graphics::xenos;
@@ -2335,6 +2368,7 @@ bool CommandProcessor::ExecutePacketType3_REG_TO_MEM(memory::RingBuffer* reader,
   mem_addr &= ~0x3;
   reg_val = GpuSwap(reg_val, endianness);
   memory::store(memory_->TranslatePhysical(mem_addr), reg_val);
+  NfsmwCpPublishEvent();  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410)
 
   return true;
 }
@@ -2351,6 +2385,7 @@ bool CommandProcessor::ExecutePacketType3_MEM_WRITE(memory::RingBuffer* reader,
     memory::store(memory_->TranslatePhysical(addr), write_data);
     write_addr += 4;
   }
+  NfsmwCpPublishEvent();  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410)
 
   return true;
 }
@@ -2410,6 +2445,7 @@ bool CommandProcessor::ExecutePacketType3_COND_WRITE(memory::RingBuffer* reader,
       write_reg_addr &= ~0x3;
       write_data = GpuSwap(write_data, endianness);
       memory::store(memory_->TranslatePhysical(write_reg_addr), write_data);
+      NfsmwCpPublishEvent();  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410)
     } else {
       // Register.
       WriteRegister(write_reg_addr, write_data);
@@ -2455,6 +2491,7 @@ bool CommandProcessor::ExecutePacketType3_EVENT_WRITE_SHD(memory::RingBuffer* re
   address &= ~0x3;
   data_value = GpuSwap(data_value, endianness);
   memory::store(memory_->TranslatePhysical(address), data_value);
+  NfsmwCpPublishEvent();  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0410)
   return true;
 }
 
